# GitHub MCP - NO TOKEN NEEDED
# Authentication is handled through VS Code OAuth (see README "First-Time GitHub MCP Setup").
# The .vscode/mcp.json file configures the server; no environment variables required.
# Each developer signs in individually through VS Code — no tokens to generate or store.

# Jira (Cloud or Data Center/Server)
JIRA_BASE_URL=https://jira.your-company.com
# Data Center/Server: generate a Personal Access Token from your Jira profile > Personal Access Tokens.
# Cloud: generate an API token at id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens.
JIRA_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Only required for Jira Cloud (paired with JIRA_AUTH_TOKEN as Basic auth). Leave unset for Data Center.
JIRA_EMAIL=

# Path to the target application built using this framework (absolute or relative to this project root).
# Defaults to ../bookstore-app (sibling directory). Change to point to any application you generate.
APP_PROJECT_PATH=../bookstore-app
